# netsurf: a conversion walk whose subtree a script removed stops cleanly (patch 437)
# Generated 2026-11-22
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 436)
#
# The first box conversion builds 100 nodes a slice and the main loop runs
# the page's timers between slices. A script that removes the subtree the
# walk is inside left it reading nodes whose parent chain ends at a
# parentless node, with no box above: no containing block. That was a NULL
# dereference in box_construct_element (props.containing_block->type), the
# containing-block assert in box_construct_text, box_add_child's `parent`
# assert at an inline's close (guardian's one abort, 428) and next_node's
# `parent != NULL` on the climb.
#
# Where the walk should go on is lost with the subtree, so the walk stops:
# the node builds nothing (box_construct_note_detached sets
# ctx->walk_detached and logs once), next_node returns NULL from then on,
# an inline closing outside the document puts its INLINE_END in the line
# its box opened in, and at completion box_construct_close_inlines gives
# every inline the walk left open its INLINE_END, so the tree laid out
# until the rebuild is whole. A nodeless mark (macos9_js_mark_dom_dirty)
# asks for the full rebuild, which runs once the content is READY.
#
--- a/content/handlers/html/box_construct.c
+++ b/content/handlers/html/box_construct.c
